    "definition": "AVM is a three-lens journaling scaffold for grief, gratitude, and gentle momentum: Mementō amāre (remember to love/protect), Mementō vīvere (remember to live—one tiny act), Mementō mortuōrum (remember the dead—carry the story). Use it to keep bonds, act softly, and honor limits. Professional note: AVM is a user-originated working pattern (non-canonical) presented here for practical use.",
    "help": "Walk the triangle each day. Amāre: who/what you’ll actively love or protect. Vīvere: one reversible act of living you can finish now. Mortuōrum: a memory vignette + one gratitude line. Green/green/green → proceed; yellow → adjust; red → soften or rest. Use letter-writing to a loved one or past self if it helps.",
