    "definition": "The Eisenhower Matrix is a time-management and decision tool that classifies tasks by urgency and importance. It divides work into four quadrants: Do (urgent & important), Schedule (important but not urgent), Delegate (urgent but not important), and Eliminate (neither). It helps reduce stress, improve focus, and rebalance effort toward long-term goals.",
