      "search_text": "self-consistency & semantic-entropy gate self-consistency-semantic-entropy-gate a production-grade pre-display gate that samples k candidates, measures self-consistency and semantic entropy, and then selects, abstains, or revises according to policy. it balances exploration (temperature, top-p) with reliability, explains decisions in plain language, and logs revisions for audits. describe the protected route, then choose k, diversity knobs (temperature, top-p), an agreement rule, an entropy strictness, and abstain/revision/tie-break policies. every select offers none and other. use notes fields to specify numeric thresholds or custom logic. the output block computes scores, explains choices, and produces a final decision. lens:secular lens:western level:advanced origin:arxiv-org origin:deepmind-com origin:github-com persona:advocate persona:business-analyst persona:business-intelligence-analyst persona:citizen persona:community-member persona:data-analyst persona:engineer persona:facilitator persona:organizer persona:public-relations-manager persona:qa-engineer persona:site-reliability-engineer persona:user-experience-researcher persona:user-experience-researcher persona:volunteer topic:abstention topic:ensemble topic:self-consistency topic:semantic-entropy topic:uncertainty type:framework use:evaluation use:gatekeeping use:pre-display-check evaluation testing quality reliability analytics operations safety governance route / use-case summary k — number of samples temperature top-p (nucleus sampling) agreement rule agreement notes semantic-entropy threshold entropy notes abstain policy abstain notes revision policy (on failure) revision notes tie-break strategy tie-break notes additional notes & numeric thresholds"
