    "definition": "An informal Magic-Quadrant-style scaffold: define axis rubrics with explicit anchors and weights, score vendors, normalize if needed, and place them on Ability to Execute (Y) × Completeness of Vision (X) with clusters and uncertainty.",
    "help": "Fill scope and ICP. Write 5–8 criteria for each axis as ‘Name=weight — anchors: 0…, 3…, 5…’. Paste vendors (one per line) with exec and vision scores like ‘Reliability=4’. Pick normalization, clustering, and visual encodings. The output returns a clean placement table, quadrant labels, rubric anchors, and next moves.",
