    "definition": "A complete scaffold that moves from situational read (3C) to segment choice and position (STP) to a 4P/7P marketing mix with evidence and metrics.",
    "help": "Fill top to bottom. In 3C, be candid: strengths, constraints, unit economics, and channels you actually control. In STP, list candidate segments, then score them with a clear rubric before you pick a primary and secondaries. Write a positioning sentence using target, outcome, frame of reference, point of difference, and reasons to believe. In 4P/7P, map each P back to your proof pillars so execution cannot drift from the claim. Set practical KPIs, risks, and 90-day moves. Choose service intensity to toggle 4P vs 7P. Pick output depth to control verbosity.",
