    "definition": "A practical scaffold to estimate WTP, derive price bands, and quantify price-feature trade-offs using Van Westendorp, Gabor-Granger, and Conjoint.",
    "help": "Work top to bottom. State segment and context first. Choose a primary method based on your decision need: Van Westendorp for fast bands, Gabor-Granger for demand and elasticity of one offer, Conjoint for multi-attribute price-feature trade-offs and market simulation. Use the design fields to define price points, attributes, tasks, and sample sizes. Add unit cost so the profit view is explicit. Enter outputs as you compute them: bands, demand points, utilities, and WTP deltas. Finish with decisions: list price, fences, packages, and forecast. Use Outline only for facilitation, Table + labels for working docs, and Full canvas for executive-ready detail.",
