    "definition": "A practical scaffold for selecting and building Central or Peripheral persuasion routes based on audience motivation and ability, then measuring durable attitude and behavior change.",
    "help": "Start by diagnosing Motivation (relevance, stakes, accountability, need for cognition) and Ability (knowledge, time, attention, distractions). If both are high, go Central: lead with the best issue-relevant arguments and evidence. If one or both are low, either raise ability (scaffold) or use ethical Peripheral cues and a low-effort next step while you build toward Central. Always separate cues from core arguments and measure outcomes that matter.",
