    "definition": "COM-B states that a behavior occurs only when Capability, Opportunity, and Motivation are sufficient; use it to diagnose the limiting factor and map to the Behaviour Change Wheel, intervention functions, and named behavior change techniques.",
    "help": "Start with the behavior: who does what, when, and where. Diagnose which element is constraining performance now: Capability (physical or psychological), Opportunity (physical or social), or Motivation (reflective or automatic). Map each bottleneck to intervention functions from the Behaviour Change Wheel and specify concrete techniques using the BCT Taxonomy v1. If the barrier sits above the individual, add policy levers. Measure success at the behavior level. Keep claims testable and ethical.",
