    "definition": "FBM states that a target behavior happens only when Motivation, Ability, and a Prompt converge at the same moment; design by lowering ability costs, placing the right prompt, and not relying on volatile motivation.",
    "help": "Start with a specific behavior. Score ability using the six simplicity factors: time, money, physical effort, brain cycles, social deviance, and non routine. Remove the largest blocker first and make the action tiny. Choose a prompt type that fits current motivation and ability: Signal, Facilitator, or Spark. Place the prompt at the moment of relevance. Measure first action rate, prompt to action latency, and tiny streaks. Escalate difficulty only after reliability is established.",
