    "definition": "A practical playbook from the Behavioural Insights tradition: if you want a behavior, make it Easy, Attractive, Social, and Timely—auditing journeys and testing lever-specific changes.",
    "help": "Start by defining the behavior and audience. Audit the journey step by step. For each step, write concrete changes under Easy, Attractive, Social, and Timely. Prioritize Easy first (defaults, fewer steps, plain language). Add Attractive (salience, incentive clarity), Social (norms, commitments, messenger), and Timely (fresh starts, just-in-time reminders) moves. Change one lever at a time in tests. Pair EAST with a root-cause model like COM-B so you fix capability and opportunity constraints, not just messaging.",
