    "definition": "A diagnostic and design scaffold for communication: name a fixable exigence, target the audience who can act, work with constraints, and deliver a fitting response at the right moment.",
    "help": "Start with the situation, not the slogan. Write a one line exigence that names the imperfection and the modification you seek. Identify the audience who both can be moved and can act, plus the legitimizers they heed. Inventory constraints such as facts, rules, values, time, channels, and credibility. Choose a purpose, genre, tone, and kairos window that fit. Draft only what the actor needs to decide or do now. Test for fit with a reasonable actor standard and remove anything that is not needed under the constraints. Use the Bitzer versus Vatz selector to decide how much you will set salience versus accept the given situation.",
