    "definition": "A dispute diagnostic and agenda scaffold that locates where the hang-up is: Conjecture (facts), Definition (classification), Quality (evaluation), then Policy (action). Settle lower stases before arguing higher ones.",
    "help": "Start by asking participants which stasis they believe the dispute is at. Write a one-line claim for each stasis and stop at the first one that breaks. Structure the meeting in stasis order: Conjecture, then Definition, then Quality, then Policy. Match evidence to stasis: data for Conjecture, criteria or precedents for Definition, benchmarks and values for Quality, options and owners for Policy. Close each stasis with a decision record such as We agree the facts show X. Park arguments that jump ahead. Export a decision log and assign owners and dates.",
