    "definition": "A practical editing scaffold that rewrites lists, pairs, headings, and CTAs into parallel grammatical structures so readers parse faster, compare fairly, and remember more.",
    "help": "Paste your messy list. Choose a frame (Verb + Object, Noun phrase, or Gerund + object). Provide a base verb or a gerund seed if needed. The template prints a parallel draft, shows length balance, and gives quick repairs for correlative pairs, comparisons, headings, and CTAs. Finish with the quality checklist. Use parallelism where scanning matters (menus, bullets, tables, headings).",
