      "search_text": "rasa–dhvani planner (sanskrit poetics → modern comms) rasa-dhvani-planner a practical scaffold for choosing one dominant rasa (aesthetic mood) and realizing it through suggestion (dhvani) across words, visuals, and pacing. pick a primary rasa, set causes/signs (vibhāva/anubhāva/vyabhicāribhāva), write for suggestion, guard the mood, and close with a felt action. every select has an escape option. leave fields blank to use defaults. type:framework level:intermediate use:planning use:writing use:storytelling use:messaging lens:eastern scope:self scope:pair scope:team scope:organization scope:community scope:society persona:product-manager persona:product-marketer persona:ux-writer persona:content-designer persona:educator persona:policy-communicator writing rhetoric storytelling tone primary rasa (dominant mood) supporting rasa (optional) context audience goal (behavior/decision) vibhāva (determinants/setting) anubhāva (expressions/signs) vyabhicāribhāva (supporting feelings) dhvani cues (what to imply, not say) key verbs (parallel, mood-aligned) mood breakers to remove cta (felt action) inclusivity & ethics notes proof plan (how you’ll judge fit)"
